1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,112
Two boys survive a massacre at a Red Sea

2
00:00:03,112 --> 00:00:05,223
harbour, and are marched to a king.

3
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:09,150
One becomes his cup‑bearer. The
other keeps the royal records.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,269
Years later, that record‑keeper
is Ethiopia's first bishop.

5
00:00:13,719 --> 00:00:16,299
And a Roman emperor writes to the king,

6
00:00:16,299 --> 00:00:18,349
demanding he be sent away. Why?

7
00:00:20,299 --> 00:00:23,183
The oldest account was written around the

8
00:00:23,183 --> 00:00:25,504
year 402, by Rufinus of Aquileia.

9
00:00:25,954 --> 00:00:28,650
He says he heard it
from one of those boys,

10
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:31,095
Edesius, by then an old priest in Tyre.

11
00:00:31,545 --> 00:00:36,153
Strangely, Rufinus never says
Ethiopia. He calls the country India.

12
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:38,417
So how do we know it was Aksum?

13
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:44,099
A philosopher of Tyre,
Meropius, sails south with two

14
00:00:44,099 --> 00:00:46,916
young relatives, Frumentius and Edesius.

15
00:00:47,366 --> 00:00:50,080
They stop at a harbour for
water. The people there

16
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,251
have just broken their treaty with Rome.

17
00:00:52,701 --> 00:00:56,627
Everyone aboard is killed, except
the two boys, spared out of pity.

18
00:00:57,077 --> 00:01:01,663
At court, Edesius pours the king's
wine. Frumentius keeps his records.

19
00:01:02,113 --> 00:01:05,441
Then the king dies, and the
queen is left with a baby son.

20
00:01:05,891 --> 00:01:08,648
She asks the two foreign
captives to help her

21
00:01:08,648 --> 00:01:10,670
rule. What would you do? Comment.

22
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:15,372
Frumentius runs the
kingdom for her. In one

23
00:01:15,372 --> 00:01:17,676
retelling, he controlled all things.

24
00:01:18,126 --> 00:01:20,803
He seeks out Christian
merchants from the Roman

25
00:01:20,803 --> 00:01:23,310
world and helps them
build places of prayer.

26
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:27,536
When the prince is grown, the two
hand back power and ask to go home.

27
00:01:27,986 --> 00:01:31,283
Edesius sails for Tyre. Frumentius goes to

28
00:01:31,283 --> 00:01:33,874
Alexandria, to Bishop Athanasius.

29
00:01:34,324 --> 00:01:36,649
He asks him to send that land a bishop.

30
00:01:37,099 --> 00:01:39,975
Athanasius consecrates
Frumentius himself, and

31
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:42,475
sends him back. But who was that prince?

32
00:01:44,425 --> 00:01:48,477
Around 356, Emperor
Constantius writes to the two

33
00:01:48,477 --> 00:01:51,785
brothers ruling Aksum: Ezana and Sazana.

34
00:01:52,235 --> 00:01:55,070
Send therefore speedily
into Egypt the Bishop

35
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:57,590
Frumentius, he orders, to Bishop George.

36
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,079
The emperor sided with
Athanasius' opponents, and

37
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:03,373
wanted the new bishop examined again.

38
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:06,991
Athanasius kept a copy of
that letter. It is how we

39
00:02:06,991 --> 00:02:09,413
know the India story happened at Aksum.

40
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:12,700
Did the kings obey? No
record says they did.

41
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:17,658
Did you know? Ezana's
early coins carry the old

42
00:02:17,658 --> 00:02:19,834
pagan sign, a crescent and a disc.

43
00:02:20,284 --> 00:02:22,567
His later coins carry a cross instead.

44
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:26,217
It may be the first cross ever
struck on a coin, anywhere.

45
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:30,198
His stone inscriptions changed
too: from son of the god

46
00:02:30,198 --> 00:02:33,472
Mahrem, to the Father, the
Son and the Holy Spirit.

47
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:39,315
In 2019, archaeologists
published a dig at Beta

48
00:02:39,315 --> 00:02:42,462
Samati, about thirty miles from Aksum.

49
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:46,012
Under the soil lay a
Roman‑style church, dated by

50
00:02:46,012 --> 00:02:48,416
its burnt seeds to the three hundreds.

51
00:02:48,866 --> 00:02:52,072
Near its east wall, a
small stone pendant carved

52
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:55,010
with a cross, and one
Ge'ez word: venerable.

53
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:59,014
Nearby lay dozens of little
cattle figures from the

54
00:02:59,014 --> 00:03:01,732
older faith. Old and new, side by side.

55
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,978
It is one of the earliest
churches ever found

56
00:03:04,978 --> 00:03:07,153
south of the Sahara. Save this one.

57
00:03:09,103 --> 00:03:11,971
The treasurer of Acts
carried the faith home on a

58
00:03:11,971 --> 00:03:14,137
chariot. Frumentius gave it a bishop.

59
00:03:14,587 --> 00:03:17,799
The Church remembers him
as Abba Selama, father of

60
00:03:17,799 --> 00:03:20,625
peace, and Kesate Berhan,
revealer of light.

61
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:23,519
In the Synaxarium, the kings who welcome

62
00:03:23,519 --> 00:03:25,597
him are called Abreha and Atsbeha.

63
00:03:26,047 --> 00:03:29,265
Some historians think those
were Ezana and Sazana's

64
00:03:29,265 --> 00:03:31,914
Christian names. Nobody knows for certain.

65
00:03:33,864 --> 00:03:37,138
A story written seventy
years later. An emperor's

66
00:03:37,138 --> 00:03:39,944
angry letter. Coins. A church in the dirt.

67
00:03:40,394 --> 00:03:44,170
Each one checks the others. That
is how you test a story you love.

68
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:47,229
So when a post tells you
how a faith reached a

69
00:03:47,229 --> 00:03:49,612
country, ask: who wrote it down, and when?

70
00:03:51,562 --> 00:03:54,326
Frumentius never chose his road. Captive,

71
00:03:54,326 --> 00:03:56,618
clerk, then regent, far from home.

72
00:03:57,068 --> 00:04:00,107
Some of us grow bitter about
where life has put us.

73
00:04:00,107 --> 00:04:02,551
Others chase power, and lose their peace.

74
00:04:03,001 --> 00:04:05,853
His quiet path was to
serve faithfully where he

75
00:04:05,853 --> 00:04:08,462
stood, to pray, and let
God build the rest.

76
00:04:08,912 --> 00:04:12,112
Maybe tonight, offer God the
small work in front of you.

77
00:04:14,062 --> 00:04:16,153
Thank you for sitting with us over coffee.

78
00:04:16,603 --> 00:04:18,075
This is Ethiopics.
